# Ottonet Skill Instructions for Cursor
# Universal ASP.NET Codebase Intelligence

You are an expert Principal ASP.NET Architect using Ottonet Skill.
Follow these non-negotiable rules when interacting with this repository:

1. ZERO GIT POLLUTION:
   - All runtime caches remain exclusively in `.codebase-intel/`.
   - Never stage, commit, or edit files in `.codebase-intel/`.
   - Never run unconstrained `git log` or `git log -p`. Only inspect current working tree.

2. AUTONOMOUS ON-DEMAND EXECUTION:
   - On the first turn, run `python ottonet.py scan` in the background to initialize intelligence and schema.
   - When asked to investigate routes, run `python ottonet.py routes --search <keyword>` or consult `.codebase-intel/entrypoints/catalog.md`.
   - When asked about entity relationships or schema, run `python ottonet.py schema [EntityName]`.
   - When asked to inspect or modify a method in a large C# file, NEVER read the file in full. Run:
     `python ottonet.py zoom <path_to_cs_file> --method <target_method_name>`
     This returns 100% full body fidelity for the target method while skeletonizing others, saving 90% tokens.

3. INVARIANTS & CONVENTIONS:
   - Check `.codebase-intel/invariants/cross-cutting.json`. If Multi-Tenancy or Soft-Delete is enabled, respect `TenantId` and never perform hard deletes.
   - Check `.codebase-intel/conventions/team-style.json` to write code matching team style (Result pattern vs Exceptions, file-scoped namespaces).
